# Compiled search binaries. Build them with search/orderly/Makefile instead of
# committing them: they are redundant with the sources, add non-diffable blobs
# to history, and nothing would enforce that a committed binary still matches
# the .c file next to it. An earlier version of this PR committed `orderly` and
# `brute`; a reviewer flagged it.
zarankiewicz-3-3/search/orderly/orderly
zarankiewicz-3-3/search/orderly/brute
zarankiewicz-3-3/search/orderly/extend

# Enumeration dumps and search outputs: large, regenerable, not evidence on
# their own (the run log in EXACT_VALUES.md records the node counts).
zarankiewicz-3-3/search/orderly/*.txt
zarankiewicz-3-3/search/orderly/*.out
